        {
          "type": "modopedia:text",
          "x": 2,
          "y": 16,
          "width": 96,
          "line_height": 9,
          "text": "A center rune is the semantic entry point of an array, but the final effect usually comes from the operation tree inside it. Fire, Water, and Mana already have direct runtime"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "integration; Earth and Wind also serve as semantic compilation centers."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• mana: with arrow parameters it launches a Manaball; arrow count affects launch data.\n• fire: the fireball center template, commonly combined with FireProjectileOp."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• water: the center for water projectiles and collision-triggered behavior.\n• wind / star: rotation-capable templates suited to direction and local-frame experiments."
    },
    {
      "type": "modopedia:text",
      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 96,
      "line_height": 9,
      "text": "• dark / earth / space: registered center roles whose effects depend on matched operation definitions."
    },
